# Responsive Breakpoint Standards - MANDATORY

## Standard Breakpoints (EXACT Values Required)

```css
/* Mobile Portrait */
@media (max-width: 480px) {
  /* Single column, touch-optimized */
}

/* Mobile Landscape / Small Tablet */
@media (min-width: 481px) and (max-width: 768px) {
  /* Transitional layout */
}

/* Tablet */
@media (min-width: 769px) and (max-width: 1024px) {
  /* Multi-column, larger touch targets */
}

/* Desktop Small */
@media (min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 1200px) {
  /* Full desktop features */
}

/* Desktop Large */
@media (min-width: 1201px) {
  /* Maximum width containers */
}
```

## Breakpoint Implementation Rules

### Mobile-First Approach - MANDATORY
- Start with mobile styles (no media query)
- Enhance progressively upward
- Never use max-width only (except for mobile-only styles)

### Container Behavior by Breakpoint

**Mobile Portrait (≤ 480px):**
- Single column layouts
- Full-width components
- Touch-friendly interactions (44px minimum)
- 1rem horizontal padding

**Mobile Landscape (481px - 768px):**
- May use 2-column grids where appropriate
- Maintain touch-friendly sizing
- Slightly larger spacing
- 1.5rem horizontal padding

**Tablet (769px - 1024px):**
- 2-3 column layouts
- Larger touch targets maintained
- More generous spacing
- 2rem horizontal padding

**Desktop Small (1025px - 1200px):**
- 3-4 column layouts
- Standard interaction patterns
- Full feature set
- 2rem horizontal padding

**Desktop Large (≥ 1201px):**
- Maximum container width: 1200px, centered
- Optimal spacing and typography
- 2rem horizontal padding

## CSS Custom Properties for Breakpoints

```css
:root {
  --breakpoint-mobile: 480px;
  --breakpoint-mobile-landscape: 768px;
  --breakpoint-tablet: 1024px;
  --breakpoint-desktop: 1200px;
  
  /* Container padding */
  --container-padding-mobile: 1rem;
  --container-padding-tablet: 2rem;
  --container-padding-desktop: 2rem;
  
  /* Maximum width */
  --container-max-width: 1200px;
}
```

## Component Responsive Patterns

### Header Behavior
```css
/* Mobile header - hamburger menu */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .header {
    /* Mobile navigation */
  }
}

/* Desktop header - full navigation */
@media (min-width: 769px) {
  .header {
    /* Desktop navigation */
  }
}
```

### Grid Layouts
```css
.grid {
  display: grid;
  gap: var(--spacing-md);
  grid-template-columns: 1fr; /* Mobile: 1 column */
}

@media (min-width: 481px) {
  .grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); /* Tablet: 2 columns */
  }
}

@media (min-width: 1025px) {
  .grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); /* Desktop: flexible */
  }
}
```

### Typography Scaling
```css
.title {
  font-size: 1.5rem; /* Mobile */
}

@media (min-width: 769px) {
  .title {
    font-size: 2rem; /* Tablet */
  }
}

@media (min-width: 1025px) {
  .title {
    font-size: 2.5rem; /* Desktop */
  }
}
```

## Touch Target Requirements

### Minimum Sizes
- Touch targets: 44px × 44px minimum
- Interactive elements: 48px × 48px preferred
- Text links: 44px touch area (padding/margin)

### Implementation
```css
.touchTarget {
  min-height: 44px;
  min-width: 44px;
  padding: 12px 16px;
}

@media (min-width: 1025px) {
  .touchTarget {
    /* Can be smaller on desktop */
    min-height: auto;
    min-width: auto;
    padding: 8px 12px;
  }
}
```

## Full-Width Section Pattern

```css
.section {
  width: 100vw;
  position: relative;
  left: 50%;
  right: 50%;
  margin-left: -50vw;
  margin-right: -50vw;
}

.sectionContent {
  max-width: var(--container-max-width);
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 0 var(--container-padding-mobile);
}

@media (min-width: 769px) {
  .sectionContent {
    padding: 0 var(--container-padding-tablet);
  }
}
```

## Content Layout Guidelines

### Mobile (≤ 768px)
- Single column content
- Vertical navigation
- Stacked elements
- Minimal whitespace
- Touch-optimized interactions

### Tablet (769px - 1024px)
- 2-3 column layouts
- Horizontal navigation options
- Balanced whitespace
- Hybrid touch/mouse interactions

### Desktop (≥ 1025px)
- Multi-column layouts
- Full navigation menus
- Generous whitespace
- Mouse-optimized interactions

## Testing Requirements

### Breakpoint Testing Checklist
- [ ] Layout works at exactly 480px
- [ ] Layout works at exactly 768px  
- [ ] Layout works at exactly 1024px
- [ ] Layout works at exactly 1200px
- [ ] Touch targets are ≥44px on mobile
- [ ] Text is readable at all sizes
- [ ] Navigation works at all breakpoints
- [ ] Content doesn't overflow containers

### Performance Considerations
- Use `em` units in media queries for accessibility
- Minimize breakpoint-specific CSS
- Avoid layout shifts between breakpoints
- Test with slow connections on mobile

## Common Mistakes to Avoid

❌ **Don't:**
- Use arbitrary breakpoint values
- Mix max-width and min-width inconsistently  
- Forget touch target sizing
- Use desktop-first approach
- Ignore intermediate breakpoints

✅ **Do:**
- Use standard breakpoint values exactly
- Follow mobile-first methodology
- Test on real devices
- Consider performance implications
- Design for accessibility at all sizes
